's just perfect for a show  like this and i feel that it helped make  the show a lot more entertaining than it  seemed at first the show won't blow  anyone's minds but it's a decent pick up  for the season especially if you're one  who likes rom-coms  ninth on the list is combatants will be  dispatched  okay so listen to this you've got an  obnoxious protagonist who looks like  he's had enough of life on an adventure  besides the straight-laced blonde girl  he's with our protagonist is joined by  an ambitious captain of the god a dark  mage and a chimera with cenibio  tendencies  if it sounds like some sort of konosuba  love child you're absolutely correct as  it's from the same creator from an  anecdotal standpoint  it seems that when it comes to fantasy  the same court of archetypes and  personalities to form that specific four  or five person party has proven to work  excellently i mean you do see  shades of it in the core cast of ari  furetha princess connect has something  resembling it too they all differ in  execution and for combatants will be  dispatched that comes in the form of  some tactical warfare gimmicks and a  heavy focus on lewd comedy if you're up  for something like gonosuba and want  more of the laughs and the degeneracy  from it combatants should be part of  your watch list no question  at number eight we take a look at  shadows house  shadows house is an interesting show  before the season started i praised its  overall ambiance in its victorian era  backdrop i felt that we're due for  another creepy gothic anime and so far i  think that my expectations for shadow's  house have been met the mysteries are  great and i had my ample full of  suspense from this anime and while i  wouldn't put shadows house's anime of  the season candidate i think the  cloverworks has done an overall  excellent job in bringing the series to  life seriously it just does such a good  job at captivating the audience with  those eerie supernatural elements and  the overall cinematography  you get drawn into the mystery of the  shadow's house and like a spectre the  anime just doesn't let you go once it's  in your grass i can't wait to see more  with each passing episode and as more  questions appear  with everyone that gets answered if  you're like me and if you're looking for  something chilly and mysterious this  season  has this great anime for you  [Music]  seventh in line is don't toy with me  miss nagatoro  [Music]  it's a show that i braced myself for  early on in the season but surprisingly  the reception towards nagatoro has been  pretty tame i admit that seeing  nakathora's smug face with the first few  episodes was quite addictive and i think  that in terms of the production side of  things  the show is serviceable the acting's  great and i think that the art is just  right for a show like this  i can't help but feel sorry for the poor  guy though the show has been getting a  steady increase in his fan base through  the anime adaptation and i think that a  lot of it has to do with the characters  and their antics we've seen the bullying  turning into romance thing before  still i don't think that makes it a bad  show if you're looking for a rom-com  with that premise nagatoro should  suffice in giving you your fill for the  season  number six on the list is higahiro  here's another winner that i admittedly  overlooked before the season started i  mean i figured that the premise might  not be everyone's cup of tea but after  watching the first few eps and reading  some of the source material i'd say that  higahiro is one of the best romances  that we have this season i'd also say  that you should give the show a chance  because when you do  it does shine in a lot of ways it seems  the past few years the parent chart  dynamic in anime has been gaining some  momentum despite the premise possibly  setting off some red flags  i don't find anything too questionable  about the series yep there's some minor  fan service in there but come on  are we still piling about fan service in  anime in this day and age especially  when things like ero manga sensei exists  to make whatever fan service in higger  heroes seem like child's play to be  completely honest gigahero is a very  wholesome series filled with dramatic  moments  about relationships and taking  responsibilities gigahero reminds me of  those self-help shows like domozaki or  origairu and if you want something like  that but with a parental relationship  element higahiro is the show for you  next in line is eden zero  for all the memes and jokes made about  mashima's character design decisions and  such eden zero has proved to be a pretty  cool show that deserves to be one of the  top anime of the season it's still early  but it's providing ample entertainment  for me especially as a fan of fairy tale  i'd have the fairy tale comparisons to  end with that statement because i feel  the eden zero deserves to stand on its  own as a quirky fun adventure with how  hit or miss the studio has been the past  few years jc staff has done a pretty  good job  adapting the series i didn't notice some  index tier rushing or one punch man  two-tier animation i'd say the eden  zero's not exactly the most unique anime  out there but it doesn't need to be the  tropes are there the usual mushy my hero  things are there the shonen cliches are  there but  are they automatically bad i'd say no  especially if you can put them on a  light-hearted and easy-going adventure  like this one eden zero  knows what it is and it instead focuses  its efforts on giving the fans of the  genre  exactly what they want  from a personal perspective 86 is one of  my most anticipated shows before the  start of the season it felt like a  breath of fresh air for action like  novels casual watchers would probably be  hooked by mandatory waifu character lena  the edgy feel that the trailer exudes or  the mecca and military elements  it seemed to be a renaissance of the  mecca 